  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently VRCX enables creeps to log every single version of every single avatar you ever wear without even needing to be online by exploiting the API to pull the ID from the profile photo. Apparently some people have massive databases stretching back years. This can be avoided by having VRC+ and changing your profile photo, and while I support VRChat needing to make money I feel like this privacy shouldn't be behind a paywall, especially since most people don't even know of this vulnerability, nor its solution.\n\nI propose that the avatar ID attached to profile photo is obfuscated in some way as to prevent the avatar from being looked up.\n\nOf course the obvious solution is to simply unfriend these people, but there is no way to know if someone is using VRCX or other tools that snoop the API.",
